<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Mozart is a 28-year-old composer and pianist who comes for the preventive visit booked at intake, four weeks after acute post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis was diagnosed. He finished penicillin, and furosemide was stopped two weeks ago when the swelling had gone and his blood pressure was normal. He feels well, has no swelling, and his urine looks normal. He is back to teaching and played a full concert last week. He has taken no ibuprofen. He has just moved to a larger apartment. He has never had a preventive visit as an adult and wants to catch up. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 28</td></tr><tr><td>Kidneys</td><td>No swelling; urine normal in color; weight steady at 61 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None; antibiotic course completed and diuretic stopped</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on the portal before the visit and reviewed with him face to face by Dr. Kranzler-Obi. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and better each week</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Busy and happy with his work; worried about money after the lost weeks but caught up with his pupils</td></tr><tr><td>Substance use</td><td>Two drinks at most on two or three evenings a week; never used tobacco; no drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks across the city to lessons every day; dances at parties; no structured exercise</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Eats out often; keeping salt down since the kidney illness</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Six hours on most nights; composes late</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Married, one partner; no concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Feels safe; smoke alarm in the new apartment</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Does not drive; wears a seat belt in taxis</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No problems</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

