    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan made. Tetanus booster and influenza vaccine given; HIV, hepatitis C, and hepatitis B screening drawn today. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis, recovering (N00.9)</content>. No edema and normal blood pressure off medication. Kidney labs are due at the six-week visit in two weeks, as planned. Inactivated influenza and Tdap vaccines are safe in recovering glomerulonephritis. [S]<list><item>C3, creatinine, potassium, urinalysis, and urine protein-to-creatinine ratio at the six-week visit.</item><item>Keep salt moderate; no NSAIDs.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>118/76 mmHg, normal off medication</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 2 at intake, below the threshold for men; drinking unchanged by his report</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 15 to 65; antigen-antibody test drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test for adults 18 to 79, drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel (surface antigen, surface antibody, and core antibody) drawn today; vaccination to follow if he is not immune</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and cholesterol screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>BMI 23.0 and under 35; statin assessment begins at 40</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap given today; no dose recorded in the last ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Declined</td><td>Discussed; he will decide later in the season</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision-making for adults 27 to 45; he chose not to have it</td></tr><tr><td>Skin cancer counseling and dental care</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sun protection discussed; dental visit within the year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine; Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: KDIGO 2021 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Glomerular Diseases (Kidney Int 2021;100(4S):S1-S276) (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, chronic kidney disease and hypertension monographs (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-week kidney review in two weeks with blood and urine tests. Screening results through the patient portal. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-27: six-week review: C3, kidney function, urine protein and blood, and the long-term plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
